The PRIMME sources are modified in these places:
- src/primme/src/include/common.h: MEM_POP_FRAME restores the context's
  frame pointer when the call it wraps returned an error. Without it the
  context keeps pointing at a stack frame that has gone out of scope, which
  AddressSanitizer reports as stack-use-after-scope in Mem_pop_frame.
- src/primme/src/svds/primme_svds_c.c: the functions that take a context
  from primme_svds_get_context free it on every return, including error
  returns and the early return in convTestFunATA. Without it the context's
  frame is never freed, which valgrind reports as definitely lost.
- src/primme/src/linalg/blaslapack_private.h and blaslapack.c: every 'BLAS'
  and 'LAPACK' routine taking a character argument is declared and called
  with Fortran's hidden character lengths (FC_LEN_T), as R requires.
- src/primme/src/eigs/convergence.c: under LP_CONVTEST_DECIDES (set in
  src/Makevars), the shortcut in check_convergence that flags a pair
  converged without calling the convergence test is removed.
- src/primme/src/eigs/primme_interface.c and
  src/primme/src/svds/primme_svds_interface.c: the default outputFile is
  NULL instead of stdout, so the library writes nothing to the console.

